# Knot theory and tricolorability, an invariant that tells knots apart. A knot is a closed loop in space, and the
# question is whether two loops can be deformed into each other without cutting. A three-coloring paints each arc of a
# knot diagram with one of three colors so that at every crossing the three arcs meeting there, the over-strand and the
# two under-strand pieces, are either all the same color or all three different. A coloring using more than one color is
# nontrivial, and whether a knot admits one is unchanged by the Reidemeister moves, so it is a genuine invariant. The
# trefoil admits a nontrivial coloring, painting its three arcs the three different colors so every crossing is a rainbow,
# while the unknot, a single arc, admits only one color, so the trefoil is truly knotted. This file MODELS the three
# colors and DEFINES the crossing rule as a function returning whether a crossing is legal. It PROVES the rule's laws: a
# monochromatic crossing is legal, the rainbow crossing of three distinct colors is legal, a crossing with exactly two
# colors is illegal, and the rule is symmetric in the two under-strands. The color laws are quantified over the actual
# color type and checked by induction.

# The three colors of a tricoloring.
form hue
  case red
  case green
  case blue

# Whether a crossing satisfies the tricoloring rule.
form check
  case legal
  case illegal

# The tricoloring crossing rule: given the over-strand color and the two under-strand colors, a crossing is legal when the
# three are all the same or all three different, and illegal otherwise, which is exactly the case of two colors meeting.
task cross
  take over, like hue
  take under-a, like hue
  take under-b, like hue
  like check
  fork case, read over
    case red
      fork case, read under-a
        case red
          fork case, read under-b
            case red
              send back
                make legal
            case green
              send back
                make illegal
            case blue
              send back
                make illegal
        case green
          fork case, read under-b
            case red
              send back
                make illegal
            case green
              send back
                make illegal
            case blue
              send back
                make legal
        case blue
          fork case, read under-b
            case red
              send back
                make illegal
            case green
              send back
                make legal
            case blue
              send back
                make illegal
    case green
      fork case, read under-a
        case red
          fork case, read under-b
            case red
              send back
                make illegal
            case green
              send back
                make illegal
            case blue
              send back
                make legal
        case green
          fork case, read under-b
            case red
              send back
                make illegal
            case green
              send back
                make legal
            case blue
              send back
                make illegal
        case blue
          fork case, read under-b
            case red
              send back
                make legal
            case green
              send back
                make illegal
            case blue
              send back
                make illegal
    case blue
      fork case, read under-a
        case red
          fork case, read under-b
            case red
              send back
                make illegal
            case green
              send back
                make legal
            case blue
              send back
                make illegal
        case green
          fork case, read under-b
            case red
              send back
                make legal
            case green
              send back
                make illegal
            case blue
              send back
                make illegal
        case blue
          fork case, read under-b
            case red
              send back
                make illegal
            case green
              send back
                make illegal
            case blue
              send back
                make legal

# A MONOCHROMATIC CROSSING IS LEGAL: painting all three arcs one color satisfies the rule, cross(h, h, h) = legal, for
# every color h. This is the trivial coloring, always available, which is why every knot including the unknot is at least
# one-colorable. Proved by induction over the three colors.
rule a-monochromatic-crossing-is-legal
  seat h, like hue
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call cross
        read h
        read h
        read h
      make legal
  fold h

# THE RAINBOW CROSSING IS LEGAL: three different colors at a crossing satisfy the rule, cross(red, green, blue) = legal.
# This is the crossing of the trefoil's nontrivial coloring, where its three arcs take the three colors, so the trefoil is
# tricolorable.
rule the-rainbow-crossing-is-legal
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call cross
        make red
        make green
        make blue
      make legal
  calm hold

# A TWO-COLOR CROSSING IS ILLEGAL: exactly two colors meeting, cross(red, red, green) = illegal, breaks the rule. This is
# why the unknot has no nontrivial coloring: its single arc forces two colors to meet illegally, so only the monochromatic
# coloring survives, and tricolorability separates the trefoil from the unknot.
rule a-two-color-crossing-is-illegal
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call cross
        make red
        make red
        make green
      make illegal
  calm hold

# THE RULE IS SYMMETRIC in the two under-strands: swapping them does not change legality, cross(over, a, b) = cross(over,
# b, a), for all colors. So the crossing rule does not depend on which under-strand is named first, as an invariant must
# not. Proved by simultaneous induction over the three colors.
rule the-crossing-rule-is-symmetric
  seat over, like hue
  seat under-a, like hue
  seat under-b, like hue
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call cross
        read over
        read under-a
        read under-b
      call cross
        read over
        read under-b
        read under-a
  fold over, under-a, under-b
